    "title": "Stale github-reads.md in consumer repos references non-existent scripts/safe_ingest.py",
    "labels": [],
    "body": "## Problem\n\nAfter migrating from the submodule model to the daemon workspace plugin (PR matthewmcneill/esp32-app-foundation#291), consumer repos still have a stale `.agents/rules/github-reads.md` that tells agents to run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/safe_ingest.py issue-view <number>\n```\n\nThis path doesn't exist in the consumer repo \u2014 `safe_ingest.py` lives in the daemon plugin at `~/.gemini/config/plugins/bug-fixer-daemon/workspace-plugin/bug-fixer/scripts/safe_ingest.py`.\n\n## Current Behaviour\n\n- Agents following the repo's `github-reads.md` rule try `python3 scripts/safe_ingest.py ...` \u2192 fails (file not found)\n- The `bug-fixer-command-gate` hook eventually blocks the fallback `gh` commands and prints the correct path in the deny message, so agents can recover \u2014 but only after a wasted round-trip\n\n## Expected Behaviour\n\nThe daemon's own [`rules/github-reads.md`](https://github.com/matthewmcneill/bug-fixer-loop-plugin/blob/main/workspace-plugin/bug-fixer/rules/github-reads.md) already has the correct instructions (it tells agents to use the path from the gate's deny message). The consumer repo's copy should either:\n\n1. **Be deleted** \u2014 the daemon plugin ships the rule, so the repo copy is redundant, or\n2. **Be updated** to match the daemon's version\n\n## Affected Repos\n\n- `matthewmcneill/esp32-app-foundation` (discovered during PR #291 review)\n- Potentially any other consumer repo that was previously enrolled via the submodule\n\n## Context\n\nDiscovered during code review of matthewmcneill/esp32-app-foundation#291.",
